<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chanda Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1240 CE – 1751 CE (approx.) · capital Chanda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gond kingdom of eastern Maharashtra ruled from Chanda (Chandrapur), whose fortified capital and temples survive.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> chiefs built a kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wainganga-river">Wainganga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wardha-river">Wardha</a> valleys from around the 13th century, traditionally beginning with Kol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhil</a> or Bhim Ballal Singh at Sirpur. The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ballarpur">Ballarpur</a> and then, in the 15th and 16th centuries under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandkya-ballal-shah">Khandkya Ballal Shah</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrapur">Chanda</a>, where a walled city was laid out.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> kings ruled forested and farming country through Gond and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> nobles, and gradually adopted Rajput-style kingship and Hindu temple patronage. The Mahakali temple and the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrapur">Chandrapur</a> date from this period. The kingdom paid tribute at times to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> and later to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, while keeping wide local autonomy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 18th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhonsles">Bhonsle</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a> extended their power over the region, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrapur">Chanda</a> was annexed around 1751. It passed with Nagpur to the British in 1853. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> rulers survive as part of local memory and architecture.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1240 CE – 1751 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.38%;width:10.17%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1240 CE – 1751 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chanda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Khandkya Ballal Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Gond religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gondi, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gonds of Chanda, Kingdom of Chandrapur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1496&amp;focus=chanda-kingdom" aria-label="Chanda Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7050 1333 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chanda Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7370 1589L7126 1652"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7126 1652h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7370 1589h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7370 1589h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Chanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1496&amp;focus=chanda-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

